# This file exists to stop npm falling back to the repository .gitignore.
#
# Without it, npm uses the root .gitignore when a package has no .npmignore.
# That root file ignores `dist/` — which is correct for git and catastrophic
# for publishing, because `prepublishOnly` builds `dist/` and package.json
# points `main` and `types` at `dist/index.js` and `dist/index.d.ts`.
#
# This is not hypothetical. The same class of root-anchored ignore rule
# silently shipped Python wheels containing no code at all. The build tools
# exit 0 on an empty artefact, so nothing fails loudly: you only find out when
# someone installs the package and the import fails.
#
# Anything listed below is excluded from the published tarball. `dist/` and
# `src/` are deliberately absent from this list. Verify before every publish:
#
#     npm pack --dry-run
#
# and confirm dist/index.js is present and non-empty in the file listing.

examples/
tsconfig.json
*.tsbuildinfo
*.test.ts
*.spec.ts
.DS_Store
